export const LEGAL_TERMS_MARKDOWN = "# Informed Ministries App — Terms of Use\n\n**Draft for legal review — not yet in force**\nVersion 0.1 · Prepared 7 September 2026\n\nThese Terms of Use (\"Terms\") are an agreement between you and Informed Ministries (ABN [insert ABN]) (\"Informed Ministries\", \"we\", \"us\", \"our\"), which operates the Informed Ministries mobile and web application (the \"App\"). By creating an account or using the App you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains how we handle your personal information and forms part of these Terms.\n\n## 1. What the App is, and what it is not\n\nThe App is an independent spiritual formation resource for Adventist believers. It provides Bible reading, reading plans, devotional series, Sabbath School lesson material, writings from Adventist pioneers and Ellen G. White, and small-group tools for Bible study.\n\n**The App is not a counselling, medical, mental health or crisis service.** Some content in the App speaks to grief, anxiety, loss, illness and death from a Scriptural perspective. That content is offered for reflection and encouragement only. It is not professional advice, and it is not a substitute for care from a doctor, psychologist, counsellor, pastor or crisis service.\n\n**If you are in immediate danger, call 000. If you are in distress or having thoughts of harming yourself, contact Lifeline on 13 11 14 (Australia) or your local emergency or crisis service.** We may show these contacts in the App; we cannot monitor conversations or respond to emergencies.\n\nThe App is also not an official service of the Seventh-day Adventist Church or the General Conference of Seventh-day Adventists. Official Sabbath School lesson material is provided through a third-party service (Adventech) and reproduced with attribution; the App itself is independently operated by Informed Ministries.\n\n## 2. Who can use the App\n\nYou must be at least 13 years old to create an account. If you are under 18, you may use the App only with the consent and supervision of a parent or guardian, and your parent or guardian agrees to these Terms on your behalf.\n\n**Kids mode** is a restricted experience for younger children within a parent's or guardian's account. It does not create a separate account for the child, does not provide access to community features, and does not collect information from the child beyond what is described in the Privacy Policy. The parent or guardian is responsible for supervising a child's use of the App.\n\n**Small groups and video rooms are for adults only.** You must be 18 or over to create or join a small group, and you confirm this when you do so. We may remove any person from a group, or close a group, if we reasonably believe this requirement is not met.\n\n## 3. Your account\n\nYou are responsible for keeping your login details private and for everything done through your account. Tell us promptly at [support email] if you believe someone else has accessed it.\n\nYou may delete your account at any time from within the App or by contacting us. Deleting your account removes your personal data as described in the Privacy Policy.\n\n## 4. Content in the App\n\n### Scripture and third-party material\n\nBible text, Sabbath School lessons, devotional series and other material in the App come from a range of sources. Some are in the public domain (for example the King James Version, and writings by Ellen G. White and Adventist pioneers first published before 1929). Others are used under licence or with permission (for example Sabbath School lesson content via Adventech, and *Our Daily Bread* devotionals with the permission of Our Daily Bread Ministries). Each is credited where it appears.\n\nYou may read, listen to and share content from the App for personal, non-commercial devotional use. You may not copy, republish, sell or distribute licensed content outside the App, or remove attributions or copyright notices.\n\n### Editorial notes\n\nShort notes labelled \"A note from Informed Ministries\" are written by Informed Ministries. They are our own reflections and are not statements of official church doctrine.\n\n### Accuracy\n\nWe take care with what we publish, but we do not warrant that any content is complete, current or free of error. Scripture is the authority; the App is a tool for reading it.\n\n## 5. AI-generated content\n\nThe App uses artificial intelligence in two ways.\n\n**Answering your questions.** Features such as **Ask the Bible** and the **Sabbath School Study Tutor** generate a response to what you type.\n\n**Generating study material.** When you use the study generator (the sparkle icon) on a topic page, or open features such as Explain This Verse, Deep Dive chapter context, cross-references, daily topic reflections, or a reading plan marked as AI-generated, the material you see is created by AI — either on your request or in advance for that topic or passage.\n\nFor all of it, you acknowledge that:\n\n- **AI content is framed from a Seventh-day Adventist understanding of Scripture.** We instruct the AI to answer in keeping with Adventist teaching, including on subjects such as the Sabbath, the state of the dead, and the sanctuary. That framing is a setting we have chosen; it does not make any response an official statement of the Seventh-day Adventist Church, and people from other traditions should read responses with that in mind.\n- AI content is generated automatically and **may be inaccurate, incomplete or mistaken**, including on matters of Scripture, history and doctrine — and may at times fail to reflect Adventist teaching despite that framing.\n- AI content is not the teaching of Informed Ministries or of any church, and is not pastoral, theological, medical or legal advice.\n- A study or lesson generated for you is **not reviewed by a person before you see it**. Test it against Scripture, and check it with a pastor or trusted teacher before teaching it or sharing it with others.\n- AI features are not a means of contacting a person. They cannot recognise or respond to an emergency.\n\nWhere a screen shows AI-generated content, the App identifies it as such. Content that is not AI-generated — Scripture, Sabbath School lessons, licensed devotionals, pioneer and Ellen G. White writings, and notes labelled \"A note from Informed Ministries\" — is identified by its source where it appears.\n\n## 6. Small groups, video rooms and your conduct\n\nSmall groups are private spaces created by members of the App for Bible study. The person who creates a group (the \"host\") controls who joins, can remove members, and can end a video session.\n\nWhen you take part in a group, you agree to:\n\n- treat other members with respect, and keep to the group's purpose of Bible study;\n- not share another member's name, image, words or invite code outside the group without their permission;\n- not record video sessions without the clear consent of everyone present;\n- not use groups to harass, threaten, deceive, solicit money from, or exploit anyone, or to promote any commercial venture;\n- not post anything unlawful, sexually explicit, hateful or abusive, or anything you do not have the right to share.\n\nAnything you post in a group is your responsibility. We do not review group content before it is posted and do not moderate video sessions live. Hosts and members can report conduct to us, and we may remove content, remove people from groups, or suspend or close accounts where we reasonably believe these Terms have been breached. Video sessions are not stored by us.\n\n## 7. Your content\n\nReflections, journal entries, notes and anything else you write in the App remain yours. You give Informed Ministries a limited licence to store and display that content in order to provide the App to you (and, for group posts, to other members of that group). We will not publish your private content or use it for advertising.\n\n## 8. Availability and changes\n\nThe App is provided free of charge and depends on third-party services (including hosting, database, video and content providers) we do not control. We do not promise the App will be available at all times or without interruption, and we may change, suspend or withdraw features at any time.\n\nWe may update these Terms. If we make a material change we will tell you in the App before it takes effect. Continuing to use the App after that date means you accept the updated Terms.\n\n## 9. Your rights under Australian law\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes, restricts or modifies any consumer guarantee, right or remedy you have under the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that cannot be excluded by agreement. The limitations in section 10 apply only to the extent permitted by law.\n\n## 10. Liability\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by law:\n\n- The App and its content are provided \"as is\". We exclude all warranties, conditions and representations not expressly stated in these Terms.\n- Informed Ministries, and the people who run it, are not liable to you for any loss or damage (including indirect or consequential loss) arising from your use of, or inability to use, the App or its content, including reliance on any content or AI response, or from the conduct of any other user.\n- Where liability cannot be excluded but can be limited, our liability is limited, at our option, to re-supplying the relevant service or paying the cost of having it re-supplied.\n\nYou agree to indemnify Informed Ministries against any claim or loss arising from your breach of these Terms or your conduct towards other users.\n\n## 11. Ending your use\n\nYou can stop using the App and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or end your access if you breach these Terms, if required by law, or if we withdraw the App. Sections 4, 7, 9, 10 and 12 continue to apply after your access ends.\n\n## 12. General\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia, and you agree to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of its courts. If any part of these Terms is found to be unenforceable, the rest continues to apply. These Terms and the Privacy Policy are the whole agreement between you and Informed Ministries about the App.\n\n## 13. Contact\n\nInformed Ministries\nABN [insert]\n[postal or email address]\n[support email]\n" as const;

export const LEGAL_PRIVACY_MARKDOWN = "# Informed Ministries App — Privacy Policy\n\n**Draft for legal review — not yet in force**\nVersion 0.1 · Prepared 7 September 2026\n\nInformed Ministries (ABN [insert]) (\"we\", \"us\", \"our\") operates the Informed Ministries mobile and web application (the \"App\"). This policy explains what personal information we collect, why, how we hold it, and your choices. We handle personal information in accordance with the Australian Privacy Principles in the *Privacy Act 1988* (Cth).\n\n## 1. What we collect\n\n**Account information.** When you create an account: your name (as you choose to give it), email address, and a password we store only in hashed form. If you sign in with a third-party provider, we receive the name and email that provider shares.\n\n**Your use of the App.** Reading-plan progress, devotional and Sabbath School progress, bookmarks, streaks, and the reflections, notes and journal entries you write. These are stored so the App can show them back to you.\n\n**Small groups.** If you create or join a group: your display name, the groups you belong to, invite codes you use, the posts you make in a group, and whether you are currently in a video session. When you join a group you confirm you are 18 or over; we record that confirmation.\n\n**AI features.** When you use Ask the Bible or the Study Tutor, the question you type (and, for the Tutor, the current lesson) is sent to our AI provider to generate a response. When you use the study generator or features such as Explain This Verse, the topic or passage is sent, not your identity. Generated study material may be stored and shown to other users who choose the same topic or passage; it is not linked to you. We may keep a record of questions and responses for a limited period to fix problems and prevent misuse.\n\n**Technical information.** Device type, operating system, app version, approximate region derived from your connection, error reports, and basic usage events (for example that a screen was opened). We use this to keep the App working and to understand which features are used.\n\n**Notification subscriptions.** If you turn on a Daily verse or Sabbath School reminder, we store the push endpoint for that browser or device, the time you chose, and your time zone. We use these only to send the reminder you asked for.\n\n**Kids mode.** Kids mode runs inside a parent's or guardian's account. We do not create a profile for the child, do not ask the child for personal information, and do not make community features available in kids mode. Progress in kids mode is stored against the parent's account.\n\nWe do not collect payment information (the App is free), precise location, contacts, or photos unless you choose to share one within a group.\n\n## 2. Why we collect it\n\nWe use personal information to:\n\n- provide the App and remember where you are up to;\n- run small groups and video sessions between members;\n- answer questions you ask AI features;\n- send you service messages (for example about changes to these terms or a security issue);\n- keep the App secure, fix errors, and prevent misuse;\n- understand, in aggregate, how the App is used so we can improve it.\n\nWe do not sell personal information, and we do not show advertising in the App.\n\n## 3. Who we share it with\n\nWe share personal information only with providers who help us run the App, and only what each needs:\n\n- **Hosting and database** — the App's server and database run on infrastructure located in Sydney, Australia ([hosting provider] and [database provider]).\n- **Video sessions** — group video is delivered by [video provider]. Audio and video pass through their servers during a session and are not recorded or stored by us.\n- **AI features** — questions to Ask the Bible and the Study Tutor are processed by [AI provider]. We send the question and the context needed to answer it, not your account details.\n- **Content providers** — Sabbath School lessons and some devotional content are fetched from third parties (for example Adventech, Our Daily Bread Ministries). We fetch content on your behalf; we do not send them your identity.\n- **Error and usage reporting** — [analytics/error provider], which receives technical information only.\n\nSome of these providers are based outside Australia, or may process data outside Australia. Where that happens we take reasonable steps to ensure they handle your information in a way consistent with the Australian Privacy Principles.\n\nWe may also disclose personal information where the law requires it, or to protect the safety of a person.\n\n## 4. Group members\n\nOther members of a group you join can see your display name, your posts in that group, and whether you are in a live session. They cannot see your email address, your private notes or reflections, or your activity outside the group. Please think of group content as shared with those members, and do not share personal information about other members outside the group.\n\n## 5. How long we keep it\n\nWe keep your information while your account is active. If you delete your account, we delete your personal information and content within 30 days, except where we must keep records to meet a legal obligation or resolve a dispute. Backups are overwritten in the ordinary course. Group posts you made remain visible to the group in anonymised form (\"Former member\") unless the host removes them. Notification subscriptions (the endpoint, the time you chose, and your time zone) are deleted when you turn the reminder off, and they are deleted with your account.\n\nRecords of AI questions are kept for no longer than [30] days.\n\n## 6. Security\n\nWe protect personal information with measures including encrypted connections, hashed passwords, access limited to those who need it, and hosting in an Australian region. No system is completely secure. If a data breach occurs that is likely to cause serious harm, we will notify you and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner as the law requires.\n\n## 7. Your choices and rights\n\n- **Access and correction.** You can view and change most of your information in the App. For anything else, contact us and we will provide access or correct it within a reasonable time.\n- **Deletion.** You can delete your account from the App, or ask us to.\n- **Groups.** You can leave a group at any time; the host can remove members.\n- **AI features.** You can use the App without ever using AI features; they only process what you type into them.\n- **Complaints.** If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, contact us first. If we cannot resolve it, you can complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at oaic.gov.au.\n\n## 8. Children\n\nThe App is not directed at children under 13 for account creation. Kids mode is designed for children to use under a parent's or guardian's supervision within the parent's account, and we do not knowingly collect personal information directly from a child. If you believe a child has provided us personal information without a parent's consent, contact us and we will delete it.\n\n## 9. Changes\n\nWe may update this policy. If we make a material change we will tell you in the App before it takes effect.\n\n## 10. Contact\n\nInformed Ministries\nABN [insert]\n[postal or email address]\n[privacy contact email]\n" as const;

